// PENDING RULING (2026-07-31, claude — soak jul30a reactive divergence_000000).
// Class: arm RE-selection whose body bottoms interiorly in the wake cycle.
//   interp: Trace([0:i64:-1]; [0:i64:9]; [0:i64:-1])
//   jit:    Trace([0:i64:-1]; [0:i64:9]; [0:i64:0])
//
// Epochs: e0 in0=0,in1=false -> arm2: 0 - 1/1 = -1 (both). e1 in1=true ->
// arm1: 9 (both; arm2 sleeps). e2 in1=false,in0=1 -> arm2 RE-selected,
// v0=0, 1/v0 bottoms (div0) in the becoming-selected pass.
//
// ROOT CAUSE — the two backends carry interior op-cache memory across a
// DESELECTION differently:
// - interp: `Cached::sleep` (node/mod.rs:328) clears every interior cache
//   when the arm sleeps, but the ARM's own wrapper cache survives (select
//   sleeps `arms[j].1.node`, not the wrapper — select.rs:231). On the wake
//   pass Sub's rhs (the div) bottoms with NO cache to ride
//   (`rhs.cached.as_ref()?` -> None, op.rs:841), the body produces
//   nothing, and the becoming-selected fire emits the arm wrapper's
//   surviving cache: fired(-1) (select.rs:292).
// - kernel: the honor-gated replay site words (the jul16 interior-bottom
//   ride fix) are NOT invalidated by deselection — the div site rides its
//   e0 word (1), the body computes 1-1=0 untainted, kernel emits 0.
//
// The ride itself is agreed semantics while the arm stays CONTINUOUSLY
// selected (always-selected variant of this program agrees, riding), and
// a FIRST-ever selection with the same bottom agrees too (no stale words,
// no arm cache). Only reselect-with-history diverges.
//
// Fix requires a ruling: matching the interp needs (a) per-arm
// invalidation of interior replay/ride words on deselection AND (b) a
// per-arm value channel in kernel select state so the becoming-selected
// fire can fall back to the arm's last output when the fresh body
// bottoms — the kernel currently has neither. Alternatively rule the
// interp's clear-on-sleep the accident and make sleep preserve interior
// caches (kernel semantics win) — smaller change, but touches canonical
// node-walk sleep semantics. Repro is exercised end-to-end by the
// schedule header below; original finding annotated in the jul30a
// campaign corpus as dedup key.
// schedule-v1: cap=144 events=1152; in1=bool:true; in1=bool:false in0=i64:1
{let v0 = i64:1 - in0; select in1 {true => i64:9, _ => in0 - (i64:1 / v0)}}
